        "original_id": "f450bfa8-83b1-5302-ae23-58aab8a0070e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Ehrlichman, Richard Nixon\n- Products: The Company, Washington: Behind Closed Doors\n- Concepts: Roman à clef, political fiction\n- Organizations: Simon & Schuster, Nixon administration, Watergate scandal\n\nFacts:\n- John Ehrlichman was a close aide to President Richard Nixon and a figure in the Watergate scandal.\n- Roman à clef is French for \"novel with a key\" and describes a novel about real life presented with a façade of fiction.\n- John Ehrlichman wrote The Company as a political fiction roman à clef novel.\n- Simon & Schuster first published The Company in 1976.\n- The Company was inspired by John Ehrlichman's time with the Nixon administration.\n- Washington: Behind Closed Doors was based on John Ehrlichman's book The Company.",
